Ladybird emits U+FFFD for a decimal or hexadecimal HTML character
reference above the Unicode range, even when the digits exceed 32 bits.

Blink marks the accumulated value invalid in ConsumeHTMLEntity and
emits U+FFFD in AppendLegalEntityFor. WebKit checks for overflow in
makeEntity. Gecko emits U+FFFD for an out-of-range reference in
nsHtml5Tokenizer::handleNcrValue. Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0,
and WebKit 26.5 all returned U+FFFD for both inputs that wrapped to A
in Ladybird, &#4294967361; and &#x100000041;.
